				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/imthatoneguyirl" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3987471); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3987471&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608045214" alt="ImThatOneGuyIRL" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3987471)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/imthatoneguyirl" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3987471); return false;" >ImThatOneGuyIRL</a></span> <span class="odate time_1562793641 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 Jul 2019 21:20</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4303028">
									

<p>Alpha's entire movement method, where he stops by all the other infected except for one, who sits under the table, suggests that this might be the former family's dog.</p>
<p>The entire &quot;facial tendrils&quot; intermingling&#8230; could this be the infected's version of &quot;kissing&quot;?</p>
<p>As for the infecteds around a well, with the little girl. It reminds me of the games children tend to play in European villages, occasionally around wells.</p>
<p>These infected, could they be doing the same things they normally do before infection?</p>
<p>&#8230;and are they even aware of their current state?</p>

